    {"comment": "Generic slot -> category PRIORS as graph data. A RolePrior node carries (slot, category, proper_category). The typed-new-concept rules read these via NodesWhere(RolePrior, slot, <slot>) so the category an unknown is typed with is graph-resident, not Python. The proper_category is the category to use when the orthographic cue says proper_noun (capitalized, no determiner) -- e.g. an agent that is a NAME is a person. The expected_categories LIST is the SET of categories a correctly-sensed filler may have (an agent is a person OR animal); the sense-selection rule (sense_selection_rules.py) reads it via In(Attr(cand,'category'), RolePrior.expected_categories) to score word-sense / translation candidates -- the multi-category counterpart of the single `category` prior used for typing."},
